From 40891b65b45732942a52e70e8baeb19f029c9fd5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joel Goddard <Joel.Goddard@arm.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Feb 2024 10:30:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 06/28] fix(drivers/arm/rse) force rse comms embed in RME
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

RSE COMMS pointer access protocol is not support with RME enabled as
pointers could have NS, S, RT or RM access permissions and this is not
currently supported on RSS. Therefore when RME is enabled rse comms
should always use the embed protocol.

Change-Id: Ice48b14ae139d5bcfa607a36bf901a0f68b0400c
Signed-off-by: Joel Goddard <joel.goddard@arm.com>
Signed-off-by: Nishant Sharma <nishant.sharma@arm.com>
(cherry picked from RD-INFRA-2025.07.03 commit
 f19b6b50b29583e00d3818cea2201331b1416074)
[Michał Iwanicki: test ENABLE_FEAT_RME. Upstream splits ENABLE_RME
 into ENABLE_FEAT_RME and ENABLE_RMM, and defines only those two in C.
 The realm attestation key request of the RMM then uses the embed
 protocol, which the RD-INFRA RSE answers. On the RD-V3 FVP, the pointer
 access protocol halted the RSE in tfm_hal_system_halt().]
Signed-off-by: Michał Iwanicki <michal.iwanicki@3mdeb.com>
---
 drivers/arm/rse/rse_comms.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/arm/rse/rse_comms.c b/drivers/arm/rse/rse_comms.c
index b0a5470f7..7a17f59fd 100644
--- a/drivers/arm/rse/rse_comms.c
+++ b/drivers/arm/rse/rse_comms.c
@@ -39,6 +39,13 @@ static uint8_t select_protocol_version(const psa_invec *in_vec, size_t in_len,
 	size_t out_size_total = 0;
 	size_t i;
 
+	#if ENABLE_FEAT_RME
+	/* Force use of embeded protocol as RSS_COMMS_PROTOCOL_POINTER_ACCESS
+	 * is not supported in RME.
+	 */
+	return RSE_COMMS_PROTOCOL_EMBED;
+	#endif /* ENABLE_FEAT_RME */
+
 	for (i = 0U; i < in_len; ++i) {
 		in_size_total += in_vec[i].len;
 	}
-- 
